  "summary": "I added a \"Lights off\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`. Clicking it switches to a dim, cool night look and relabels the button \"Lights on\". Clicking again restores the warm look. `typecheck` passes with the temporary test line removed.\n\nIn the night look the room goes dark, but the interior glow and a dial light stay on. The clock face stays readable in the render I checked. I didn't click the button in a browser. To see the night look I forced it on at startup for one render, then removed that line. So the real click path and the relabelling are untested, and I never rendered the final code with the lights on. A render taken before the night-look edit had also come out dark, so I couldn't tell whether the warm look is still as bright as before. I also lowered the neutral environment light from 0.35 to 0.3, so the warm look is slightly dimmer than the first version.\n\n`window.__TASK_STATE__ = { lightsOn, pendulumAngleDeg }` is set at startup and updated every frame. `pendulumAngleDeg` is the signed pendulum angle from vertical, in degrees, and swings between ±8.6° (±0.15 rad)."
}